<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reapers' War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1640–1659</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Catalan Revolt · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-spanish-war-1635-1659">Franco-Spanish War (1635–1659)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Reapers' War was a revolt of Catalonia against the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iv-of-spain">Philip IV of Spain</a>. Provoked by the billeting of royal troops and the policies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaspar-de-guzman-count-duke-of-olivares">Count-Duke of Olivares</a>, it began with the killing of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> by reapers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> in June 1640. The Catalans placed themselves under the French crown, but Barcelona surrendered in 1652, and in 1659 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roussillon">Roussillon</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cerdanya">Cerdanya</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reapers-war.jpg" alt="Reapers' War" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pandolfo Reschi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalla_de_Montju%C3%AFc_de_1641.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
